«
@@ DMOMarkov — demo of the Probability section: a Markov chain. By
@@ default an economy with three states, growth (G), stagnation (S) and
@@ recession (R), and illustrative quarterly transition probabilities;
@@ or the square transition matrix given on the stack, each row summing
@@ to 1 (states then numbered). 200 quarters are simulated from state 1
@@ and drawn as steps; below, the share of time spent in each state
@@ (gray bars) against the stationary distribution π (black lines), the
@@ solution of π·P = π with Σπ = 1. Returns both, observed and π.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @ The transition matrix, if given; any other object is left alone
  0
  If Depth 1 > Then Drop Dup TypeName End
  → dmmty
  «
  If dmmty "array" == Then
    Dup Size 1 Get → dmmq « 1 dmmq For dmmj dmmj →Text Next dmmq →List »
  Else
    [[ 0.85 0.10 0.05 ] [ 0.30 0.55 0.15 ] [ 0.20 0.30 0.50 ]]
    { "G" "S" "R" }
  End
  → dmmP dmml
  «
  dmmP Size 1 Get 200
  → dmmn dmmlen
  «
    @ The stationary distribution: (Pᵀ - I)·π = 0, the last equation
    @ replaced by Σπ = 1
    dmmP TRN dmmn IDN -
    1 dmmn For dmmj dmmn dmmj 2 →List 1 Put Next
    dmmn 1 →List 0 CON dmmn 1 Put
    Swap /
    → dmmpi
    «
      @ The chain: dmmlen states, from state 1
      1
      → dmms
      «
        1 dmmlen For dmmt
          RAND 0 1
          → dmmu dmmc dmmk
          «
            dmmP dmms 1 2 →List Get 'dmmc' Sto
            While dmmc dmmu < dmmk dmmn < And Repeat
              dmmk 1 + 'dmmk' Sto
              dmmc dmmP dmms dmmk 2 →List Get + 'dmmc' Sto
            End
            dmmk 'dmms' Sto
          »
          dmms
        Next
        dmmlen →List
      »
      → dmmtr
      «
        @ The share of time in each state
        dmmn 1 →List 0 CON
        1 dmmlen For dmmt
          dmmtr dmmt Get → dmmk « Dup dmmk Get 1 + dmmk Swap Put »
        Next
        dmmlen 1. * /
        → dmmf
        «
          ClearLCD
          "Markov chain: " dmmlen →Text + " quarters" +
          { #0d #0d 0 true false } DrawText
          @ The path, in steps: state k at height 30 + 50(k-1)/(n-1)
          1 dmmlen For dmmt
            dmmt 1 - 376 * dmmlen / 20 + IP R→I
            dmmt 376 * dmmlen / 20 + IP R→I
            dmmtr dmmt Get 1 - 50 * dmmn 1 - / 30 + IP R→I
            → dmmx0 dmmx1 dmmy
            «
              dmmx0 R→B dmmy R→B 2 →List dmmx1 R→B dmmy R→B 2 →List DrawLine
              If dmmt dmmlen < Then
                dmmx1 R→B dmmy R→B 2 →List
                dmmx1 R→B dmmtr dmmt 1 + Get 1 - 50 * dmmn 1 - / 30 + IP R→I R→B 2 →List
                DrawLine
              End
            »
          Next
          1 dmmn For dmmk
            dmml dmmk Get
            { #2d } dmmk 1 - 50 * dmmn 1 - / 22 + IP R→I R→B + { 0 true false } +
            DrawText
          Next
          @ The shares: gray bars observed, black lines stationary
          "Time share: observed (bars) / stationary π (lines)"
          { #0d #100d 0 true false } DrawText
          1 dmmn For dmmk
            400 dmmn / dmmk 0.5 - * IP R→I
            dmmf dmmk Get 100 * 220 Swap - IP R→I
            dmmpi dmmk Get 100 * 220 Swap - IP R→I
            → dmmx dmmyf dmmyp
            «
              0.5 Gray Foreground 16 LineWidth
              dmmx R→B #220d 2 →List dmmx R→B dmmyf R→B 2 →List DrawLine
              'Foreground' Purge 2 LineWidth
              dmmx 24 - R→B dmmyp R→B 2 →List dmmx 24 + R→B dmmyp R→B 2 →List DrawLine
              'LineWidth' Purge
              dmml dmmk Get " " +
              dmmf dmmk Get 100 * 0 RND R→I →Text + "/" +
              dmmpi dmmk Get 100 * 0 RND R→I →Text + "%" +
              dmmx 40 - R→B #222d 2 →List { 0 true false } + DrawText
            »
          Next
          dmmf 3 RND "observed" →Tag
          dmmpi 3 RND "stationary" →Tag
        »
      »
    »
  »
  »
  »
»
